    "moedB": "",
    "syllabus": "This course provides an in-depth exploration of data science, tracing its evolution from traditional data analysis to its current role as a critical interdisciplinary field at the intersection of computer science, statistics, and domain expertise. As data science continues to drive innovation across technology, healthcare, and finance, this course emphasizes the importance of not only extracting meaningful insights from complex datasets but also ensuring that these insights are trustworthy and relevant to the specific context in which they are applied. Through the concept of veridical data science, which integrates human judgment and domain knowledge, students will learn to produce data-driven results that are not only accurate but also reliable and ethical, addressing real-world challenges with robust and context-sensitive solutions.  Student Outcomes: 1.\tUnderstand and apply quantitative models in pricing analytics and revenue management, including newsvendor models, demand forecasting, and network revenue management. 2.\tAnalyze and optimize strategies for revenue management in various industries, such as e-retail, transportation, and hospitality. 3.\tDevelop skills to model and s",
