    "syllabus": "As industrial competition continues to accelerate AI innovations, this course will focus on the fundamentals of what has made these innovations possible, by investigating the complex roles of data, compute, and algorithms.  Unlike most AI courses which focus only on algorithmic advancement, the course will take a balanced approach and include in our survey the varied ways in which data, data analysis, and human computing has been a key part of the progress, as well as the availability of compute with scalable architectures - all three have played equally important roles in the advancement of AI. Student Outcomes 1.\tTo survey the history of AI from the perspective of how we got to where we are today, large generative models capable of completing tasks that 5 years ago were considered decades off.",
